{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1562166877,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0NjM4MTEwODM=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3510","origin":"github"},"title":"Support IPFS special remote","message":"I've been playing around a bit with [git-annex's IPFS special remote][annex-ipfs].  The special remote implementation is documented as experimental and from 2015, but it still seems to work as advertised.\n\n```\n$ git annex whereis one\nwhereis one (1 copy) \n  \t97de50fe-d40e-45e6-bd29-6c307ed4971b -- [ipfs]\n\n  ipfs: ipfs:QmUB9Nr7RpqNYQpyh4W9r3RQNttiPQ6BQ9iQLkw9LztJFz\nok\n$ git annex get one\nget one (from ipfs...) \nSaving file(s) to .git/annex/tmp/SHA256E-s4--2c8b08da5ce60398e1f19af0e5dccc744df274b826abe585eaba68c525434806\n 4 B / 4 B [================================================================] 100.00% 0s\n(checksum...) ok\n(recording state in git...)\n```\n\nBut if I try to `datalad get` the a file from IPFS, DataLad doesn't think anything needs to be done.\n\n```\n$ git annex drop --force one\ndrop one ok\n(recording state in git...)\n$ datalad -f json_pp get one\n{\n  \"action\": \"get\",\n  \"path\": \"/tmp/gx-ipfs-HZmC5Wq/one\",\n  \"status\": \"notneeded\",\n  \"type\": \"file\"\n}\n$ git annex whereis one\nwhereis one (1 copy)\n  \t97de50fe-d40e-45e6-bd29-6c307ed4971b -- [ipfs]\n\n  ipfs: ipfs:QmUB9Nr7RpqNYQpyh4W9r3RQNttiPQ6BQ9iQLkw9LztJFz\nok\n```\n\nI think IPFS is a pretty neat option for people that want to share public data without setting up external hosting somewhere, so it'd be great to make DataLad work with the IPFS special remote.\n\n[annex-ipfs]: https://git-annex.branchable.com/special_remotes/ipfs/","files":null}]}